00\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, SEPTEMBER 13, 2006\r\rMayor Washburn called the meeting to order at 7:00 p.m. in Conference Room No. 2, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Washburn, Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, Councilmembers Maurer, Wolfson.\r Absent: Councilmember Groveman.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles.\r\rCLOSED SESSION\r\rThe City Council recessed at 7:06 p.m. into closed session to confer with legal counsel regarding the following:\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Two matters of Initiation of Litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section 54956.9(c). \r\rPending litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section 54946.9(a), City of Calabasas v. RCS II Development Company, et al.� BC 339068. \r\rReal property negotiations, pursuant to Government Code Section 54956.8\r Agency Negotiator: Maureen Tamuri, Community Development Director\r Negotiating parties: City of Calabasas and Spotlight the Arts\r Instruction: Discussion regarding terms of real estate development with Spotlight the Arts. \r Identity of property: Assessor�s Parcel Numbers 2068-003-900; 2068-003-901\r\rConference with Labor Negotiator, pursuant to Government Code 54957.6\r City Negotiator: Anthony Coroalles, City Manager and Michael G. Colantuono, City Attorney\r All Unrepresented Employees\r\rThe City Council reconvened at 7:30 p.m. from closed session and Mayor Washburn called the meeting to order at 7:40 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Washburn, Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, Councilmembers Groveman, Maurer, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Bartlett, Colantuono, Coroalles, Gdala, Parker, Peirce, Rubin, Tamuri.\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Tom Gdala.\r\rMichael G. Colantuono, City Attorney, stated that the Council did not take any action which required reporting. \r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\rThe City Council concurred to approve the agenda with Items #5 and #8 being pulled off the consent calendar. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson announced that Maureen Tamuri, Community Development Director received a �Women who mean business� award. Mayor pro Tem Bozajian announced the upcoming Pumpkin Festival on October 22, 2006. Councilmember Maurer stated that two elementary schools in Calabasas, Chaparral Elementary and Bay Laurel Elementary, have been recognized as excellent schools in this month�s issue of Los Angeles Magazine. Mayor Washburn spoke regarding the League of California Cities Conference that took place in San Diego the first week of September. He spoke regarding the Dream Big bracelet campaign.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r Ben Nilsson, Los Angeles, spoke in opposition to the resolution in support of Proposition 86, �The Tobacco Tax Act of 2006�.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r\r Approval of the minutes for the July 19, 2006 City Council meeting. \r\r Recommendation to approve a professional services agreement with Martin & Chapman Co. for election consulting services for the March 6, 2007 General Municipal Election in an amount not to exceed $31,000. \r\r Authorization to execute a professional services agreement with Ms. Lori Goor for as-needed clerical and administrative services support.\r\r Recommendation to approve an amendment to an agreement with Shane�s Inspiration in an amount not to exceed $985,000.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1039, amending the policy for contributing to the funding of Community Service Organizations and rescinding Resolution No. 2005-985. \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1040, amending Resolution No. 95-347 to include language in the street vacation resolution to provide for the transfer of storm drains.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1041, in support of SB 1613 (Simitian), the California Wireless Automobile Safety Act of 2006.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1042, in support of Proposition 86, �The Tobacco Tax Act of 2006�.\r\r Approval of salary adjustment for the position of Public Works Director/City Engineer.\r\r \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1044, establishing employee flex credit amounts for 2007 benefits and rescinding Resolution No. 2005-965.\r\rCouncilmember Maurer \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to approve Consent Items #1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 9, and 10. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Groveman was absent. \r\rFollowing discussion, Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, to approve Consent Item #8. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Groveman was absent. \r\rPUBLIC HEARING\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1043, finding the City of Calabasas to be in conformance with the Congestion Management Program, and adopting the Local Development Report, in accordance with California Government Code Section 65089.\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Mayor Washburn opened the public hearing.\r\r Tom Gdala, Assistant Transportation Planner, presented the staff report. \r\r Mayor Washburn closed the public hearing.\r\r The City Council concurred to adopt Resolution No. 2006-1043, finding the City of Calabasas to be in conformance with the Congestion Management Program, and adopting the Local Development Report, in accordance with California Government Code Section 65089. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Groveman was absent.\r\r Waive further reading and introduce Ordinance No. 2006-224, amending the User's Guide and Chapter 22, Affordable Housing, of Title 17 of the Calabasas Municipal Code, as necessary to bring the City's Density Bonus provisions into conformance with the affordable housing laws of the State of California.\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Mayor Washburn opened the public hearing.\r\r Tom Bartlett, Planning Manager, presented the staff report. \r\r Mayor Washburn closed the public hearing.\r\r Mayor pro Tem Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer to continue the public hearing to September 27, 2006. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Groveman was absent.\r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS\r\r Recommended work plan for General Plan update.\r\r Tom Bartlett, Planning Manager, presented the staff report.\r\r The City Council provided direction to staff regarding the formation of the General Plan Advisory Committee.\r\rNEW BUSINESS \r\r Motion to waive further reading and introduction of Ordinance No. 2006-228, amending Section 1.16 and 8.20 of Title 8 of the Calabasas Municipal Code regarding abatement of nuisances and recovery of abatement costs.\r\rSparky Cohen, Building Official, presented the staff report.\r\rMayor pro Tem Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to waive further reading and introduce Ordinance No. 2006-228, amending Section 1.16 and 8.20 of Title 8 of the Calabasas Municipal Code regarding abatement of nuisances and recovery of abatement costs. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Groveman was absent.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r Check Register for the period of July 13, 2006 to August 29, 2006.\r\rNo Action Taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS\r\r Councilmember Wolfson provided an update on the Civic Center Project Bid.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\r City Manager Coroalles spoke regarding an upcoming phone survey that will be conducted of residents in the Greater Mulwood area regarding improvements on Mulholland Highway.\r\rThe following item was heard out the order of the agenda:\r\rAdoption of Resolution No. 2006-1039, amending the policy for contributing to the funding of Community Service Organizations and rescinding Resolution No. 2005-985. \r\rFollowing discussion, Councilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, adopted a revised Resolution No. 2006-1039, amending the policy for contributing to the funding of Community Service Organizations and rescinding Resolution No. 2005-985. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Groveman was absent.\r \rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\r\r There were no future agenda items.\r\rADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 9:02 p.m. in the memory of Marni Elise Levine.\r\r\r\r____________________________________ \rGwen Peirce, Assistant City Clerk\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 4 -\u0015\r09/13/06\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 4 -\u0015\r09/13/06\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0